      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): filter non-string env entries instead of silently deleting the entire env block",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: When a cron schedule config contains a non-string environment variable (e.g. `env: { DEBUG: true }`), the normalization function returns `undefined` — causing the caller to **silently delete the entire env block**, including any valid entries. Fixes #105433.\n\n**Solution**: Change invalid-entry handling from bail-out to skip — non-string values are filtered out while valid string entries are preserved. An env record where ALL entries are invalid still returns `undefined` (triggering deletion).\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nValidates actual production `normalizeCronJobCreate` function:\n\n```\n$ npx tsx _validate-cron-env.mts\n=== normalizeCronJobCreate — non-string env filtering ===\n\n  ✓ all-string env preserved: {\"DEBUG\":\"true\",\"NODE_ENV\":\"production\"}\n  ✓ mixed env keeps string entries\n  ✓ all-invalid env triggers deletion\n  ✓ no env normalizes ok\n\n✅ All checks passed\n```\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- Existing cron normalization test suite passes\n- Focused test file `normalize.test.ts` covers the mixed env behavior\n\n/cc @openclaw/clawsweeper",
        "branch": "fix/cron-env-nonstring-guard",
